@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Not available"; }
<h1>Not available</h1>
<p>You do not have access to that.</p>

@* The operator console refuses for two different reasons - no role, or a
   session that did not use a second factor - and from here they look identical.
   Pointing at the two-factor page costs nothing to someone without the role
   (it just shows their own status) and saves an operator from concluding the
   grant did not work. *@
<p class="muted">
    If you hold the Operator role, the console also requires that this sign-in used your
    authenticator. <a asp-controller="Security" asp-action="TwoFactor">Check your two-factor status</a>.
</p>
